<p>The email, name and password are needed for an account: without them we cannot create one. The IP address, browser and device are recorded at every sign-in, because without them we cannot protect the account from someone else getting in. The device fingerprint is optional: without consent we do not compute it. Ordering a plan also needs the choices in the order — without them we cannot conclude the contract.</p>

<h2>What “HWID” means here</h2>
<p>Browsers do not give websites the hardware ID of your computer. So by “HWID” we mean a device fingerprint: a hash of details the browser shows to every website — platform, number of cores, memory, colour depth, touch screen and graphics card (vendor and model). Besides the hash we keep a short description: system, browser, screen size, cores, memory, graphics card and time zone (for example “Windows, Chrome 128, 1920 × 1080, 8 CPU”).</p>
<p>The fingerprint is computed only if you gave consent with the separate box at sign-up — it is not ticked in advance and is not a condition for the account or the trial. It is then computed at sign-up and at sign-in from a browser used only by consenting accounts, and kept on a sign-in with the correct password to such an account (also when a two-factor code is asked for after it); a wrong password keeps none. Without consent no fingerprint is computed or kept, and the device cookie serves only sign-in security — linked accounts use neither the cookie nor a fingerprint. You can withdraw consent at any time under “Security” in your account with one click; we then delete the fingerprint we keep, and device descriptions keep only system and browser. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing before it. If JavaScript is off, signing up and signing in work without it.</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>We use only cookies the service cannot work without or cannot be secured without. The one exception is the extra purpose of the device cookie — spotting repeated trials and shared accounts: for it we ask for consent with a separate box at sign-up (see the section on HWID above). We have no advertising, analytics or third-party cookies, so we show no consent banner.</p>
