<h2>Who else sees the data</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Hetzner Online GmbH, Germany — the server Korpora runs on, in a data centre in the European Union. The database backups are kept there too.</li>
  <li>Sendinblue SAS (Brevo), France — sending the emails listed under “Emails” below.</li>
  <li>Have I Been Pwned — when you choose a new password, we send only the first 5 characters of its SHA-1 hash to check whether the password has leaked in a breach. The password and the full hash never leave the server.</li>
  <li>The bank the transfer goes through — it receives the payment details (the payer's name and account, the amount) and processes them as a separate controller under its own legal obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>The country of an IP address comes from a DB-IP database (<a href="https://db-ip.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IP Geolocation by DB-IP</a>, licence <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>) stored on our server — the IP address is not sent anywhere. We do not sell data or share it for advertising. We do not transfer personal data outside the European Union; if a Brevo sub-processor processes data outside the EU, the transfer is protected by standard contractual clauses (Art. 46 GDPR).</p>

<h2>Emails</h2>
<p>We send only emails about your account and contract: confirming your email and an email change (with a notice to the old address), password reset and password change, sign-in from a new device, wrong sign-in codes, wrong passwords or codes when confirming an action in your account, turning two-factor protection on and off, a reminder <%= trialReminder %> before the trial ends, confirmation of an order and of a withdrawal from the contract, plan changes, a notice when someone tries to sign up with your email, an email to set your password when the team creates an account for you, and confirmation that the account was deleted. We do not send marketing emails.</p>

<h2>Automated decisions</h2>
<p>We make no decisions with legal effects by automated means alone. After <%= failedLogins %> wrong passwords or codes, signing in is locked for <%= lockFor %> — a security measure that lifts by itself. If the wrong attempts happen while confirming an action in an open session, all sessions are also ended and we email you. Only a member of our team can block an account, and the reason is shown when you try to sign in.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>Connections are HTTPS only. Passwords are stored as Argon2id hashes, two-factor secret keys are encrypted, sessions live on the server and end at once when the password changes or the account is blocked. The admin panel opens only with two-factor protection. Application logs contain no emails, IP addresses or passwords, and the web server keeps no request log — it records an IP address only in its error log, when a request cannot be served.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and portability. Much of it works directly from your account:</p>
<ul>
  <li>“Profile” — correct your name and email;</li>
  <li>“Data” — download all your data as a JSON file (profile, projects, plan and orders, devices, sign-ins, sessions and the audit log entries about you) and delete the account together with your projects;</li>
  <li>“Security” — active sessions, the devices used to sign in and withdrawing consent to the fingerprint.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Right to object.</strong> You may at any time object, on grounds relating to your particular situation, to the processing of your data based on legitimate interest — the sign-in history, the device, blocking and the audit log. We then stop, unless we have compelling legitimate grounds that override your interests or the data is needed for legal claims.</p>
<p>For anything else, write to <a href="mailto:<%= privacyEmail %>"><%= privacyEmail %></a> — we answer within one month. You have the right to lodge a complaint with the Bulgarian Commission for Personal Data Protection: 2 Prof. Tsvetan Lazarov Blvd., Sofia 1592, <a href="https://www.cpdp.bg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.cpdp.bg</a>, or with the supervisory authority of the EU country where you live (in Italy, the Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).</p>

<h2>Minors</h2>
<p>Korpora is a professional tool and is not meant for people under 16.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If we change this policy materially, we will tell you by email before the change takes effect. The date of the last change is at the top of the page.</p>
